<p align="center"><b><font face="Arial" size="6"><u>Dreamweaver Application Process</u></font></b></p>

<blockquote>
  <blockquote>
    <blockquote>

<p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="4"><b>1. Make sure you have read our <a href="charter.asp">Charter</a>
and our <a href="rules.asp">Rules</a>!</b></font></p>

<p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="4"><b>2. Applicants to Dreamweavers
MUST be Level 50 or higher at time of application.&nbsp;</b></font></p>

<p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="4"><b>3. Entry to the guild is obtained
by gathering 1 Sponsor who is responsible to guide and assist the applicant in
finding guild groups and activities to attend in order to build a rapport among
our Family. Every applicant will need a total of 5 'YES' votes to be invited. 1
Sponsor vote, 3 member votes and 1 Officer vote in confirmation.&nbsp;<br>
<br>
If any applicant obtains a &quot;NO&quot; vote, they Shall not be invited into
the guild, despite having the necessary 'YES' votes.&nbsp;<br>
<br>
If an applicant receives one or more &quot;Hold&quot; votes this will
add 1 real life week to the voting process. This time will be used by the
individual posting the &quot;Hold&quot; to resolve any issues they have with the
prospective member. At the end of the additional 7 real life days the
&quot;Hold&quot; vote will be null and void. Only Yes and No Votes will be
counted at this time. If the &quot;hold&quot; vote is rescinded the prospective
member will be eligible for immediate guilding so long as all other criteria has
been met for admission.<br>
<br>
14 Real life days shall have passed from the time of Sponsorship before final
votes are tallied. This is to ensure current members have ample time to be aware
of the pending invite. Any 'No' vote acquired during this time is applied, and
that prospective member will not be invited to the guild.</b></font></p>

<p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="4"><b>4. After the 14 days are over and
you have 5 'YES' votes, one of the recruitment officers (Amiwynter, Thulal or
Aydlett) will contact you for the final screening and guild invitation.<br>
</b></font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="4"><b>5. Alternate characters shall be
invited in the guild after 14 real life days have passed. New members can
sponsor 'Prospective Candidates' and get access to our Skeleton Closet after 30
real life days have passed.&nbsp;</b></font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="4"><b>6. New members need to also have
or create a <a href="http://eq.guildmagic.com/" target="_blank">Guild Magic</a>
Roster profile prior to being accepted to the guild. Once this is done, your
character will be added to our roster.&nbsp;</b></font></p>
<p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="4"><b>7. If there is no activity on
your application for over 30 days time (from date of last post), that
application will be considered invalid and will be deleted, at which time the
applicant can choose to reapply with a clean slate and '0' votes.&nbsp;</b></font></p>
<p align="left"><b><font face="Arial" size="3">*Exceptions can be made on a case
to case basis at the discretion of an officer.*</font></b></p>
    </blockquote>
  </blockquote>
</blockquote>
